Bidi: resolve paired brackets to the direction of the run they open in

Two bugs made a closing bracket ignore its opening bracket in a right-to-left
paragraph (UAX #9 N0), so "[a coin chimes]" after an RLM drew as
"a coin chimes]]":

1. kbts__DoBreak records the last direction break (position, direction) only
   inside a branch guarded by that same record being non-zero, so it is
   never recorded and no bracket is ever resolved from the breaks; a closing
   bracket fell back to the direction of the last strong character (the
   left-to-right text inside the brackets).
2. kbts__BreakAddCodepoint maps the opening bracket's direction to a bidi
   class (L or R) for the closing bracket, then overwrites it with
   FoundBracket->Direction, a kbts_direction (DONT_KNOW 0, LTR 1, RTL 2)
   read as a bidi class (NI 0, BN 1, L 2): RTL became L.

--- a/kb_text_shape.h
+++ b/kb_text_shape.h
@@ -29330,8 +29330,7 @@
       State->LastScriptBreakScript = (kbts_u8)Script;
     }
 
-    if((Flags & KBTS_BREAK_FLAG_DIRECTION) &&
-       (State->LastDirectionBreakDirection))
+    if(Flags & KBTS_BREAK_FLAG_DIRECTION)
     {
       kbts_un LastDirectionBreakPosition = State->LastDirectionBreakPosition;
       kbts_u8 LastDirectionBreakDirection = State->LastDirectionBreakDirection;
@@ -29652,7 +29651,6 @@
           BidirectionalClass = KBTS_UNICODE_BIDIRECTIONAL_CLASS_R;
         }
 
-        BidirectionalClass = FoundBracket->Direction;
         CodepointScriptCount = 1;
         CodepointScriptOffset = BracketScript;
 
